 "notes": "Libretto by Luigi Illica and Giuseppe Giacosa (1896). Words follow the Ricordi vocal score's spelling and punctuation (Non senti?!, Poetucolo!, Momus,..., and the print's runs of dots after tue, tosto, via and poesia). Schaunard, Colline and Marcello sing the same “Momus” lines; Marcello goes on alone with “trovò la poesia!”. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, words sung on one note joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ, intervocalic s voiced. Translation literal, for meaning.",
